  "term": "cuneate nucleus",
  "definition": "The cuneate nucleus is a brain structure involved in processing sensory input after median nerve injury. In this source, it is described as showing changes in neuronal activity marker expression and as helping transmit mechanical pain-related sensations toward the thalamus.",
